            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for to sit, then the Mandarin for taxi."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 天",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "天 — tiān — \"day; sky\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "那天我们去大学了 nà tiān wǒmen qù dàxué le — That day we went to the university."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 天 (tiān) — 一 above 大: one more bar over the big piece. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "天 (tiān) is inherited from Middle Chinese then (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'the highest, with nothing above it', the sky. Its use for a day is not given there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for times and partings."
            }
          ]
        },
